      "narration_text": "Is it thirty-one times? Not here. Message eight read one point seven times what message one read, and cost about twice as much — because most of a growing session is cache: text the service has seen before and re-reads cheaply. Fifteen thousand of that forty-nine came from cache. The line overstates the bill. It does not overstate the mechanism. Every message re-reads everything, the transcript only grows, and nothing shrinks it unless you do. That's the next film.",
